/**
 * // Definition for a Node.
 * function ListNode(data, prev, next) {
 *    this.data = data;
 *    this.prev = prev || null;
 *    this.next = next || null;
 * };
 */

class Solution {
  /**
   *
   * @param {ListNode} head
   * @param {Number} X
   * @returns {ListNode}
   */
  insertBeforeHead(head, X) {
    const newHead = new ListNode(X, null, head);

    if (head !== null) {
      head.prev = newHead;
    }

    return newHead;
  }
}
```

When the list is empty, `newHead.next` remains `null`, so the result is a one-node doubly linked list. The old head is updated only when it exists.

Time complexity: `O(1)`.

Space complexity: `O(1)` extra space apart from the inserted node.

